---
import Pic from '../../components/Pic.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
import { faqSchema } from '../../lib/faq';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is this an AI keynote or a technology keynote?', a: 'Technology, with AI as the example everyone in the room is living with. The method applies to any new system, which is why it still works when the next one arrives.' },
  { q: 'Does Jack take a position on whether to adopt AI?', a: 'Yes. Adopt it the way you would hire someone: on purpose, with a job description, a manager, a probation period and a review. Fear is not a control, and neither is a ban.' },
  { q: 'How technical does it get?', a: 'As technical as the room needs. Directors get the governance questions. Operators get the probation-period mechanics. Nobody gets a tool demo.' },
  { q: 'Can the board session be combined with the keynote?', a: 'Yes. The usual pattern is the keynote for the wider audience and a closed session with the board or executive team the same day.' }
];
const page = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': site.url + '/industries/ai-emerging-technology', url: site.url + '/industries/ai-emerging-technology',
  name: 'AI and Emerging Technology Keynote Speaker | Jack P. Flaherty',
  description: 'AI and emerging technology, decided like a new hire. A job description, a manager, a probation period, a review. Keynote and board sessions by Jack P. Flaherty.',
  about: { '@id': site.url + '/#person' }
};
---
<Base title="AI and Emerging Technology Keynote Speaker | Jack P. Flaherty"
  description="AI and emerging technology, decided like a new hire. A job description, a manager, a probation period, a review. Keynote and board sessions by Jack P. Flaherty."
  path="/industries/ai-emerging-technology" image="/images/jack-p-flaherty-teaching-whiteboard.jpg" schema={[page, faqSchema(faqs)]} hero="/images/jack-p-flaherty-teaching-whiteboard.jpg">

  <section>
    <div class="wrap split top">
      <div>
        <h1>AI and emerging technology, decided like a new hire</h1>
        <p class="lede">You have the tools. Most organizations do. What you may not have is a decision anyone owns. Jack works with boards and executives on the three questions to ask before AI, or any new system, is allowed to do real work: who owns it, what is it for, how will the board know it was a success.</p>
        <h2>The decision nobody owns</h2>
        <p>AI is already in use across your organization. Some of it was approved. Most of it was not. At some point the board will ask what the controls are, and "we told people to be careful" is not one.</p>
        <p>Fear is not a control either. Banning a tool does not stop the work from happening. It moves the work somewhere you cannot see it.</p>
      </div>
      <Pic src="jack-p-flaherty-teaching-whiteboard.jpg" class="hero-img" alt="Jack P. Flaherty teaching at a whiteboard" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Fear Is Not A Control</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color:#E3D5BE">Take fear out of your organization by making the goal clear, raising transparency, encouraging curious collaboration, and then stepping back to watch your teams flourish with technology.</p>
      <div class="grid c2" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <div class="card accent"><p class="kicker">1.</p><h3>A clear goal</h3><p>Say what you are trying to accomplish before you pick a tool.</p></div>
        <div class="card accent"><p class="kicker">2.</p><h3>Governance built in</h3><p>Every technology project carries it from day one, and AI, large language models and agents most of all.</p></div>
        <div class="card accent"><p class="kicker">3.</p><h3>A repeatable framework</h3><p>One way of developing AI work, so each project strengthens the foundation for the next.</p></div>
        <div class="card accent"><p class="kicker">4.</p><h3>High-quality data</h3><p>Garbage in, garbage out. Decide what the system is allowed to learn from.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="questions">
        <h3>The four questions a board can ask</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>What is this for, and how will we know it worked?</li>
          <li>Who owns it, and what governance did it come with?</li>
          <li>Is this the same way we did the last one, or a new way every time?</li>
          <li>Where does its data come from, and would we stand behind it?</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="close">That is the whole method. It fits on one page, and a board can ask about it in four questions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Where Jack has sat</h2>
      <p>25 years in risk and advisory. 15 years at the Big Four, where he served as a director. Held CISSP, CISA and CGEIT.</p>
      <p>He has implemented and audited enterprise systems spanning cybersecurity, finance, blockchain, AI and data governance, medical records, and human resources. He served as principal consultant for California's first statewide Health Information Exchange, led PwC's healthcare risk and digital assurance work as a director, and has been interim executive and advisor to startups in fintech, blockchain and AI.</p>
      <p>He has sat with boards and audit committees while a new system went live, and he has seen which ones slept.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Ways to bring this into the room</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Keynote: Fear Is Not A Control or The Decision Switch</h3>
        <p>45 to 60 minutes, built for <a href="/keynote-speaker/fear-is-not-a-control-healthcare">health systems</a>, <a href="/keynote-speaker/fear-is-not-a-control-professional-services">professional services firms</a> or <a href="/industries/industry-associations">an association audience</a>, with one first move the room takes home.</p>
        <h3 style="margin-top:1.4rem">Board and executive session</h3>
        <p>A working session with the directors on the technology decision in front of them. <a href="/keynote-speaker/board-advisor-ai-governance">See board and executive advisory</a>.</p>
        <p>Both start with a <a href={site.calendly} target="_blank" rel="noopener">discovery call</a>. Jack replies within one business day.</p>
        <p><a class="btn" href={site.calendly} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a discovery call</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <Faq items={faqs} heading="Questions planners ask" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Cta text="Tell Jack which technology is on your agenda and who is in the room." primary={{label: 'Book Jack', href: '/book-jack'}} secondary={{label: 'See the keynote', href: '/keynote-speaker/executive-decision-making-keynote'}} />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-img { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: auto; object-fit: unset; }
  .questions { margin-top: 2rem; padding-left: 2.5rem; }
  .questions h3 { margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  .questions ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .questions li { margin: 0 0 .5rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .questions .close { margin: 1.4rem 0 0; max-width: none; white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .questions { padding-left: 1rem; } .questions li, .questions .close { white-space: normal; } }
</style>
